# Count overlapping range pairs, parsed with Match Pattern.
#
# Each line holds two ranges, "a-b,c-d". The template's named typed holes
# produce a Record per line ({a:Int, b:Int, c:Int, d:Int}); the predicate
# counts pairs whose ranges overlap at all.
#
#   domain examples/03_overlapping_shifts.domain
#   Expected output: 4
Cursed Energy: 03_overlapping_shifts.input
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
Cursed Technique: Match Pattern
    Mode: Each
    Using: "{a:int}-{b:int},{c:int}-{d:int}"
Maximum Technique: Count Matching
    Using: (r) -> r.a <= r.d and r.c <= r.b
Reveal: stdout
